    <body>
      <div type="clause" n="26">
        <head><ref type="lawCode" target="law:IICn">II Cn</ref> 26</head>
        <ab type="liebermannText" xml:lang="ang" source="#liebermann" n="26" corresp="#wit-g-a"><pb n="328" ed="#liebermann"/>And gesece se æbǽr<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="21" target="#IICn_26.lnote.oe.21"/>a þeof þ<hi rend="italic">æt</hi> þ<hi rend="italic">æt</hi> he gesece, oððe se ðe on hlafordsearwe gemet si<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="8" target="#IICn_26.lnote.oe.8"/>g, þ<hi rend="italic">æt</hi> hi<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="22" target="#IICn_26.lnote.oe.22"/>g næfre feorh n<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="23" target="#IICn_26.lnote.oe.23"/>e gesecean.</ab>
        <ab type="liebermannText" xml:lang="ang" source="#liebermann" n="26" corresp="#wit-b"><pb n="328" ed="#liebermann"/>Be ðeofan. ⁊ gesece se ebǽra ðeof þ<hi rend="italic">æt</hi> he sece, oððe se ðe on hlafordsearwe gemet sy, þ<hi rend="italic">æt</hi> hi næfre feorh ne gesecan.</ab>
        <ab type="liebermannText" xml:lang="ang" source="#liebermann" n="26" corresp="#wit-a"><pb n="328" ed="#liebermann"/>And gesece se abere ðeof þ<hi rend="italic">æt</hi> þ<hi rend="italic">æt</hi> he gesece, oððe se ðe<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="7" target="#IICn_26.lnote.oe.7-2"/> hlafordsearwe gemet sy, þ<hi rend="italic">æt</hi> hi næfre feorh ne<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="8" target="#IICn_26.lnote.oe.8-2"/></ab>
        <ab type="liebermannText" xml:lang="la" source="#liebermann" n="26" corresp="#wit-q"><pb n="329" ed="#liebermann"/>Et perquirat abere<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="13" target="#IICn_26.lnote.oe.13"/> þeof (fur probatus) quicquid perquirat, aut<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="14" target="#IICn_26.lnote.oe.14"/> qui de<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="15" target="#IICn_26.lnote.oe.15"/> morte domini sui tractauit<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="16" target="#IICn_26.lnote.oe.16"/>, nunquam sibi uitam adquirant.</ab>
        <ab type="liebermannText" xml:lang="la" source="#liebermann" n="26" corresp="#wit-inst-cn"><pb n="329" ed="#liebermann"/>Publicus latro et traditor proprii<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="10" target="#IICn_26.lnote.oe.10"/> domini, quem Angli uocant hlafordspice<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="11" target="#IICn_26.lnote.oe.11"/>, quicquid requisierint, nusquam uitam inueueniant.<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="12" target="#IICn_26.lnote.oe.12"/></ab>
        <ab type="liebermannText" xml:lang="la" source="#liebermann" n="26" corresp="#wit-cons-cn"><pb n="329" ed="#liebermann"/>Manifestus autem fur uel qui in domini prodicione extiterit, quicquid adeat usquam, nunquam salutem adquirat.</ab>
        <ab type="editionText" xml:lang="ang" source="#robertson" n="26" corresp="#wit-b"><pb n="188" ed="#robertson"/>Be ðeofan. ⁊ gesece se ebǽra ðeof þæt he sec<ptr type="editorNote" n="3" target="#IICn_26.robnote.fn.3"/>e, oððe se ðe on hlafordsearwe gemet sy, þæt hi næfre feorh ne gesecan.</ab>
        <ab type="editionText" xml:lang="ang" source="#rabin-doml" corresp="#wit-g-a"><pb n="268" ed="#rabin-doml"/>And gesece se æbæra þeof þæt þæt he gesece, oððe se ðe on hlafordsearwe gemet sig, þæt hig næfre feorh ne gesecean.</ab>
        <ab type="translation" xml:lang="de" source="#liebermann"><pb n="329" ed="#liebermann"/>(Von Dieben. <hi rend="italic">B</hi>) Und<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="1" target="#IICn_26.lnote.de.1"/> der offenkundige Dieb oder wer auf Verrath gegen seinen Herrn<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="2" target="#IICn_26.lnote.de.2"/> betroffen ist, mag [von Asylen] aufsuchen was er immer aufsuche: dass sie niemals das Leben [gesichert] erlangen.</ab>
        <ab type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude" ana="#fromGerman">(Of thieves. B) And let the manifest thief, or whoever is found guilty of treachery against his lord, seek [sanctuary] wherever he may: they are never to obtain [security of] life.</ab>
        <ab type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#robertson" corresp="#wit-b"><pb n="189" ed="#robertson"/>Concerning thieves. And the proved thief and he who has been discovered in treason against his lord, whatever sanctuary he seeks, shall never be able to save his life.</ab>
        <ab type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#rabin-doml" corresp="#wit-g-a"><pb n="269" ed="#rabin-doml"/>And anyone convicted of theft or caught conspiring against his lord shall not be able to save his life, no matter where he hides.</ab>
        <note type="comparison" source="#liebermann" n="329"><ref target="clause:IIIEg_7-3">III Eg 7.3</ref></note>
        <note type="comparisonPrinted" source="#liebermann">ebd. 7, 3</note>
        <note type="comparedBy" source="#liebermann"><ref target="clause:LeisWl_47-3">Leis Wl 47.3</ref></note>
        <note type="comparison" source="#wormald-ppmel" n="93"><label>=</label> <ref target="clause:IIIEg_7-3">III Eg 7.3</ref> <quote>III Eg 7:3 = II Cn 26</quote></note>
        <note type="editorial">A skips a line (Liebermann supplies ‘on’). Liebermann compares III Eg 7.3.; BR: added from Gesetze I p. 329, October 2026 (MS Cons)</note>
        <note type="textual" source="#rabin-doml">þæt þæt: þæt B</note>
        <note type="textual" source="#rabin-doml">gesecean: omitted A</note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="IICn_26.lnote.oe.7" n="7" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">329</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">26, 1 <hi rend="italic">fehlt</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">26, 1 lacking</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="IICn_26.lnote.oe.13" n="13" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">329</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">ob. <hi rend="italic">K;</hi> a. þ. <hi rend="italic">nur Lond</hi> (<hi rend="italic">wo</hi> f. p. <hi rend="italic">fehlt</hi>); <hi rend="italic">fehlt übrigen</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">ob. K; a. þ. only Lond (where f. p. is lacking); lacking in the others</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="IICn_26.lnote.oe.14" n="14" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">329</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de"><hi rend="italic">so Lond;</hi> uel <hi rend="italic">übrige</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">thus Lond; uel the others</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="IICn_26.lnote.oe.15" n="15" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">329</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de"><hi rend="italic">fehlt K</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">lacking in K</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="IICn_26.lnote.oe.16" n="16" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">329</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">-uerit <hi rend="italic">Hk</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">-uerit Hk</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="IICn_26.lnote.oe.21" n="21" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">328</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">æbere <hi rend="italic">Ld</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">æbere Ld</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="IICn_26.lnote.oe.8" n="8" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">328</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">sy <hi rend="italic">Ld</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">sy Ld</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="IICn_26.lnote.oe.22" n="22" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">328</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">hi <hi rend="italic">Ld</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">hi Ld</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="IICn_26.lnote.oe.23" n="23" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">328</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">ne — feorh <hi rend="italic">fehlt Ld</hi> [<hi rend="italic">wie A</hi>]</seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">ne — feorh lacking in Ld [as A]</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="IICn_26.lnote.oe.7-2" n="7" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">328</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de"><hi rend="italic">ergänze</hi> on</seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">supply on</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="IICn_26.lnote.oe.8-2" n="8" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">328</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de"><hi rend="italic">Zeile übersprungen</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">line skipped</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="IICn_26.lnote.oe.10" n="10" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">329</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">d. sui pr. <hi rend="italic">Lb</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">d. sui pr. Lb</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="IICn_26.lnote.oe.11" n="11" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">329</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">hlaue. <hi rend="italic">HDi;</hi> lauerdswiche <hi rend="italic">Lb</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">hlaue. HDi; lauerdswiche Lb</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="IICn_26.lnote.oe.12" n="12" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">329</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">26, 1 <hi rend="italic">fehlt</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">26, 1 lacking</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="erklaerung" xml:id="IICn_26.lnote.de.1" n="1" source="#liebermann-erkl"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">3</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">206</biblScope><biblScope unit="column">2</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">Gleichheit von 26. 26, 1 erklärt Einl. n. 18</seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">The identity of 26 and 26, 1 is explained in Introduction n. 18</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="erklaerung" xml:id="IICn_26.lnote.de.2" n="2" source="#liebermann-erkl"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">3</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">206</biblScope><biblScope unit="column">2</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">Herrenverrat (<hi rend="italic">s. d. Gl</hi> 7a) <hi rend="italic">u</hi>. 57 aus anderer Quelle, <hi rend="italic">u</hi>. 64 unabhängig. Inst führt dafür den technischen Ausdruck ein</seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">Treason against one's lord (<hi rend="italic">see</hi> that word in <hi rend="italic">Gl</hi> 7a) <hi rend="italic">below</hi> 57 from another source, <hi rend="italic">below</hi> 64 independently. Inst introduces the technical term for it</seg></note>
        <note type="editorNote" subtype="footnote" xml:id="IICn_26.robnote.fn.3" n="3" source="#robertson"><bibl><biblScope unit="page">188</biblScope></bibl><label>sece</label><seg type="original" xml:lang="en"><hi rend="italic">þæt þæt he gesece</hi> G, A, Ld.</seg></note>
      </div>
